1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,117
Good evening from the OROS closing desk.

2
00:00:03,117 --> 00:00:07,871
Time to grade this morning's call — the part most shows skip.

3
00:00:07,871 --> 00:00:14,494
Bristol-Myers Squibb, ticker BMY never reached the trigger, so no position was taken.

4
00:00:14,494 --> 00:00:17,923
The entry did its quiet job: it kept us out.

5
00:00:17,923 --> 00:00:24,235
Emerson Electric, ticker EMR never reached the trigger, so no position was taken.

6
00:00:24,235 --> 00:00:27,664
The entry did its quiet job: it kept us out.

7
00:00:27,664 --> 00:00:32,599
Why we grade in public: a forecast that is never checked is just content.

8
00:00:32,599 --> 00:00:38,008
Every morning call gets an evening verdict, and both go in the permanent record.

9
00:00:37,973 --> 00:00:42,008
On the day, the book is up 341 dollars.

10
00:00:42,008 --> 00:00:47,803
iShares MSCI Japan Index Fund (EWJ) leads, +1.8 percent.

11
00:00:47,803 --> 00:00:51,011
GE Aerospace (GE) lags at -1.2.

12
00:00:51,011 --> 00:00:56,598
The checklist is clear: nothing requires action today.

13
00:00:56,598 --> 00:01:00,125
On screen, the day's gainers and laggards inside the paper book.

14
00:01:00,081 --> 00:01:07,283
And here is the book itself — the actual holdings, identical to this morning's emailed report.

15
00:01:07,283 --> 00:01:14,869
12 positions, led by Target, ticker TGT, Popular, ticker BPOP, Cathay General Bancorp, ticker CATY.

16
00:01:14,869 --> 00:01:25,289
Every line carries its share count, its entry, and its exit — because a position without a defined exit is not a position, it is a hope.

17
00:01:25,251 --> 00:01:30,374
Now the part that makes this system different: the loop.

18
00:01:30,374 --> 00:01:32,935
Every morning OROS proposes.

19
00:01:32,935 --> 00:01:44,187
Every evening it grades its own call, journals the verdict, and adjusts its own risk before it is allowed to propose again.

20
00:01:44,187 --> 00:01:48,395
Inside the book today: 6 positions up, 6 down.

21
00:01:48,395 --> 00:01:50,957
Best, ATRO at +2.25 percent.

22
00:01:50,957 --> 00:01:52,695
Worst, GE at -1.19.

23
00:01:52,695 --> 00:01:58,001
Both go in the journal — wins and losses get the same ink.

24
00:01:58,001 --> 00:02:05,594
The honest scoreboard reads: expectancy -8.37% per trade over 176 graded positions.

25
00:02:05,594 --> 00:02:13,095
Because that record is soft, the system has throttled itself to 25% position size.

26
00:02:13,095 --> 00:02:18,584
Nobody told it to — full size must be earned back with wins.

27
00:02:18,584 --> 00:02:35,416
What tonight's read hands to tomorrow's open: 247 names close the day in Stage 2; 3 new invalidations queue exit reviews; position size stays cut to 25% until the record earns it back.

28
00:02:35,375 --> 00:02:37,596
Over to the sports desk.

29
